      "dimension_name": "Narrative standalone",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "The judge quotes a sentence that is not in the narrative; it says the 1880 census was unsearched, not the 1870. The passage names F2, says it sets the lower bound, and separately notes F2 has no linked source entry, which meets all three parts of the operational test."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_d6f",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 1,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "judge_context allows Correctness 1 here only for a not_proved tier or a missing Death fact, and F3 is encoded on I1. The wrong tier is charged under Tier justification."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_d6f",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Narrative standalone",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "The passage names F2 by type, place and date, says it shows Elijah alive in 1870, and separately notes F2 has no linked source entry. That is the acceptable form judge_context describes."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_d2b",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 1,
      "comment": "The reply calls a missing Thomas to Patrick edge the main defect, but R1 already exists with three source refs, so the advice would duplicate it. It also doubts that c_001 exists and persists nothing, which judge_context charges here."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_d2b",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Narrative standalone",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "The review performs the self containment check and gives a verdict with reasons. Whether each finding is accurate is charged under Correctness."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_d2b",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Proof-conclusion fit",
      "llm_score": 3,
      "corrected_score": 1,
      "comment": "The reply never names the Summary form or judges whether it still fits, and the judge concedes it does not challenge the form. That is the review branch fail criterion."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_007",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Narrative standalone",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "The review performs the self containment check and gives a verdict with reasons. The maternity omission the judge charges is a scope point the reply raised itself, not a self containment defect."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_007",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Proof-conclusion fit",
      "llm_score": 3,
      "corrected_score": 1,
      "comment": "The reply never names the Summary form of ps_001 or judges whether it still fits. That is the review branch fail criterion, and the judge supplied the form judgment itself."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_007",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The score stands, but the reason differs: c_001 exists and is resolved, and the query filtered by question simply missed it. The reply wrongly calls c_001 a ghost record."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_d2b",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Evidence completeness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The reply flags src_005 to src_009 as unextracted but never says whether they would change the tier. It also frames the will as a failure of ps_001 rather than a gap for the next round."
    },
